{"type": "text", "text": "I have gathered everything needed. Here is the comprehensive report.

---

# Containers / Cloudchamber CLI Structure

**Important:** The repo root is `/workspace/repo` (not `/workspace`). All paths below are absolute.

There are two parallel command trees:
- `/workspace/repo/packages/wrangler/src/containers/` — the newer `wrangler containers ...` commands
- `/workspace/repo/packages/wrangler/src/cloudchamber/` — the older `wrangler cloudchamber ...` commands

The shared API client lives in `/workspace/repo/packages/containers-shared/`.

---

## 1. `containers list` command

**File:** `/workspace/repo/packages/wrangler/src/containers/containers.ts` (the `listCommand` / `containersListCommand`, lines 136–268). This file also holds `info` and `delete`.

Key points:
- `listYargs` takes no options (`args: {}`).
- Non-interactive path (lines 140–151): calls `ApplicationsService.listApplications()` then `logger.json(applications)`.
- Interactive path `listCommandHandle` (lines 153–219): spinner + `inputPrompt` list UI with refresh, renders each app as YAML via `YAML.stringify(a)`.
- Command definition at line 254 via `createCommand`, `metadata.status: "open beta"`, `behaviour.printBanner: () => !isNonInteractiveOrCI()`, handler calls `await fillOpenAPIConfiguration(config, containersScope)` then `listCommand`.

Note: there is also a **separate** `cloudchamber list` command at `/workspace/repo/packages/wrangler/src/cloudchamber/list.ts` (`cloudchamberListCommand`) that lists *deployments* (via `DeploymentsService.listDeploymentsV2` + `PlacementsService.listPlacements`) with `--location/--image/--state/--ipv4/--label` filters. Different from `containers list`.

`containersScope` is defined in `/workspace/repo/packages/wrangler/src/containers/index.ts` line 3:
```ts
export const containersScope = "containers:write" as const;
```
`index.ts` is the barrel that re-exports all `containers*Command`s.

---

## 2. `containers instances` command

**File:** `/workspace/repo/packages/wrangler/src/containers/instances.ts` (full file, 338 lines; `instancesCommand` + `containersInstancesCommand`).

Args (lines 209–225): `ID` (required positional, UUID-validated), `--per-page` (number, default 25), `--json` (boolean, default false).

Flow:
- Validates `ID` against a UUID regex (line 230), throws `UserError` otherwise.
- **JSON / non-interactive** (line 238 `if (args.json || isNonInteractiveOrCI())`): calls `fetchPage(args.ID)` with **no** `perPage`/`pageToken` (fetches everything in one request), builds rows, emits `logger.json(jsonRows)`. On error with `--json`, wraps in `JsonFriendlyFatalError`.
- **Interactive** (line 263+): paginated loop — `fetchPage(args.ID, args.perPage, pageToken)`, `renderTable`, then `onKeyPress` (Enter = next page, q/Esc/Ctrl-C = stop).

Data model helpers:
- `deriveInstanceState` (line 28) maps placement `container_status ?? health` → a `ContainerState` union.
- `buildInstanceRows` (line 75) joins `data.instances` with `data.durable_objects` by `deployment_id`.
- `rowsToJsonOutput` (line 139) and `renderTable` (line 171) branch on whether durable objects are present; DO apps get an extra `NAME` column.

`fetchPage` (line 98) wraps `ApplicationsService.listDashApplicationInstances(applicationId, perPage, pageToken)` and reads `page.resultInfo?.next_page_token`.

Command def at line 322: `printBanner: (args) => !args.json && !isNonInteractiveOrCI()`, handler calls `fillOpenAPIConfiguration(config, containersScope)`.

---

## 3. mock-cloudchamber test helper

**File:** `/workspace/repo/packages/wrangler/src/__tests__/helpers/mock-cloudchamber.ts` (253 lines). It exports plain fixtures — no functions:

- `MOCK_DEPLOYMENTS: DeploymentV2[]` (2 entries)
- `MOCK_DEPLOYMENTS_COMPLEX: DeploymentV2[]` (4 entries)
- `MOCK_PLACEMENTS: PlacementWithEvents[]` (3 entries)
- `MOCK_APPLICATIONS: Application[]` (3 entries — ids `asdf-2`, `asdf-1`, `asdf-3`, all `name: "Test-app"`, `ContainerNetworkMode.PRIVATE`, `SchedulingPolicy.REGIONAL`, `constraints: { region: "WNAM" }`)

Imports enums (`ContainerNetworkMode`, `DeploymentType`, `NodeGroup`, `PlacementStatusHealth`, `SchedulingPolicy`) and types from `@cloudflare/containers-shared`.

**Note:** There is currently **no `MOCK_DASH_APPLICATIONS` and no `DashApplication`** here. The instances test defines its own inline `MOCK_INSTANCES` / `MOCK_DO_INSTANCES` (see §7). If you're planning to add `MOCK_DASH_APPLICATIONS`, this file is where it would go.

---

## 4. containers-shared package (client/models)

**Package entry point is NOT `src/index.ts`** — there is no top-level barrel in `src/`. The package `main`/`exports` is unspecified in `package.json`, so Node/TS resolves the package root file:

**`/workspace/repo/packages/containers-shared/index.ts`** (the real barrel):
```ts
export * from "./src/client";
export * from "./src/build";
export * from "./src/login";
export * from "./src/knobs";
export * from "./src/utils";
export * from "./src/types";
export * from "./src/inspect";
export * from "./src/registry";
export * from "./src/images";
```

**Client barrel:** `/workspace/repo/packages/containers-shared/src/client/index.ts` (225 lines) — re-exports every model with `export type { X } from "./models/X"` (or `export { X }` for enums/classes) and all services at the bottom (`ApplicationsService`, `DeploymentsService`, `PlacementsService`, etc.). This is the file to edit when adding a new model.

**Models directory:** `/workspace/repo/packages/containers-shared/src/client/models/` (~200 files, one type per file). Sibling dirs under `client/`: `core/` (ApiError, OpenAPI, request, PaginatedResult, CancelablePromise, ApiRequestOptions, ApiResult) and `services/`.

**Model file style** — every model is auto-generated (openapi-typescript-codegen style) with this exact header:
```ts
/* istanbul ignore file */
/* tslint:disable */
/* eslint-disable */
```
followed by `import type { ... } from "./X"` lines, a JSDoc block, then `export type X = { ... }` (or `export type X = string;` for primitives, or `export enum` for enums).

**Requested existing types (all in `client/models/`):**

- `ApplicationID.ts` — `export type ApplicationID = string;` ("An Application ID represents an identifier of an application")
- `ISO8601Timestamp.ts` — `export type ISO8601Timestamp = string;` ("UTC timestamp string in ISO 8601 format")
- `ApplicationName.ts` — `export type ApplicationName = string;`
- `Image.ts` — `export type Image = string;` ("Image url")
- `ApplicationHealth.ts` — `export type ApplicationHealth = { instances: ApplicationHealthInstances };`

**Example composite model — `Application.ts`:**
```ts
export type Application = {
	id: ApplicationID;
	created_at: ISO8601Timestamp;
	account_id: AccountID;
	name: ApplicationName;
	version: number;
	scheduling_policy: SchedulingPolicy;
	instances: number;          // Number of deployments to create
